Local research traces
=====================

Use this directory as the common entry point for project workflows. Datasets
may be stored here directly or symlinked from scratch/another disk. Everything
under traces/ is ignored by Git except this README and .gitignore, including
symlinks: each collaborator supplies their own local data location.

FreeInference
-------------

Dataset: https://huggingface.co/datasets/harvardMadsys/freeinference_agentic_trace
Pinned revision: 16d3c04dae6ccaa0c48a9064e204e3a8f1eb9ade

The shared project path is:

    traces/freeinference_agentic_trace/release/<week>/

From the repository root, link an existing download (replace the absolute path
with your own). The download root must contain release/, so link the download
root rather than release/ itself:

    ln -s /absolute/path/to/freeinference_agentic_trace traces/freeinference_agentic_trace

Alternatively, download or copy the dataset into traces/freeinference_agentic_trace/
with the same layout. Do not commit datasets or machine-specific symlinks.

Expected layout, using one week as an example:

    traces/freeinference_agentic_trace/release/2026-08-09_2026-08-15/
        manifest.json
        processed/
            requests.parquet
            sessions.parquet
            tool_calls.parquet
            tables.json
        traces/
            YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl.zst

The release contains 16 weekly directories. Keep the original compressed files
and Parquet tables; linking them does not require copying or decompressing data.
Workflows should resolve traces/ relative to the repository root and use the
shared path above, rather than embedding a collaborator's scratch path.

Check local setup from the repository root:

    test -r traces/freeinference_agentic_trace/release/2026-08-09_2026-08-15/processed/requests.parquet
    git check-ignore traces/freeinference_agentic_trace

This is the source dataset location. A FreeInference adapter is still needed
before these files can be replayed through BLIS.
